intrigue|arouse-curiosity|VERB|Arouse curiosity|To make someone curious and interested, especially because something is unusual or mysterious.|gợi sự tò mò; khiến thích thú muốn tìm hiểu|The unsigned letter intrigued the museum researcher.|Lá thư không có chữ ký khiến nhà nghiên cứu của bảo tàng tò mò.|Transitive: something intrigues someone; be intrigued by something. Intriguing describes the cause, intrigued the person.|-
pessimistic|expecting-bad-outcomes|ADJECTIVE|Expecting bad outcomes|Inclined to believe that things will go badly or are unlikely to succeed.|bi quan|Despite the clear forecast, he was pessimistic about our chances of seeing the stars.|Dù dự báo trời quang, anh ấy vẫn bi quan về khả năng chúng tôi nhìn thấy các vì sao.|Pessimistic about something; opposite optimistic. It describes an expectation rather than certainty about the outcome.|-
stubborn|refusing-to-change|ADJECTIVE|Refusing to change|Unwilling to change an opinion or decision despite persuasion.|bướng bỉnh; cố chấp|The stubborn organizer refused to move the picnic after several warnings about rain.|Người tổ chức cố chấp không chịu dời buổi dã ngoại dù đã được cảnh báo nhiều lần về mưa.|Often disapproving when applied to a person; stubborn about something. Stubbornness is the noun.|-
stubborn|hard-to-remove|ADJECTIVE|Hard to remove or resolve|Difficult to get rid of, move or deal with.|khó loại bỏ; dai dẳng|A stubborn stain remained on the carpet after two washes.|Một vết bẩn khó tẩy vẫn còn trên thảm sau hai lần giặt.|Used with problems, stains or resistance; describes persistence without implying that an object has an opinion.|-
wash|clean-with-water|VERB|Clean with water|To remove dirt from something using water, often with soap.|rửa|He washed the clay from his hands before touching the camera.|Anh ấy rửa sạch đất sét trên tay trước khi chạm vào máy ảnh.|Transitive wash something; wash dirt off something. Washed and washing are regular forms.|0
wash|clean-clothes|VERB|Clean clothes|To clean clothes or other fabric using water and a cleaning substance.|giặt|We washed the curtains before hanging them in the spare room.|Chúng tôi giặt rèm trước khi treo chúng trong phòng trống.|Wash clothes by hand or in a machine. Washable means suitable for washing.|2
wash|act-of-cleaning|NOUN|Act of washing|An occasion or process of cleaning something with water.|lần giặt; việc giặt rửa|The muddy blankets need another wash before they can be stored.|Những chiếc chăn lấm bùn cần được giặt thêm một lần nữa trước khi cất.|Countable in give something a wash or need a wash; washing also names the general activity.|1
down|towards-lower-position|ADVERB|Towards a lower position|Towards or at a place lower than the starting position.|xuống; ở phía dưới|The child climbed down carefully and handed me the kite.|Đứa trẻ trèo xuống cẩn thận rồi đưa tôi chiếc diều.|Often follows a movement verb; no noun complement is needed. Downstairs is a separate compound.|0
down|along-a-route|PREPOSITION|Along a route|Along a road, river or similar route, away from the starting point.|dọc theo; xuôi theo|We walked down the narrow lane until we reached the bakery.|Chúng tôi đi dọc con ngõ hẹp cho đến khi tới tiệm bánh.|Followed by a noun phrase: down the road. The route need not slope downward.|1
